// Title: Xwizard.EXE Execution From Non-Default Location
// Sigma ID: 193d5ccd-6f59-40c6-b5b0-8e32d5ddd3d1
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Christian Burkard (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-09-20 | Modified: 2024-08-15
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: Detects the execution of Xwizard tool from a non-default directory. When executed from a non-
//   default directory, this utility can be abused in order to side load a custom version of
//   "xwizards.dll".
// False positives:
//   - Windows installed on non-C drive
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Xwizard/
//   - http://www.hexacorn.com/blog/2017/07/31/the-wizard-of-x-oppa-plugx-style/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_xwizard_execution_non_default_location.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\xwizard.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "xwizard.exe") and (not((FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\System32\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\WinSxS\\")))
